# This also gives you a better relationship with Virtuals

Don't compete with their ACP service marketplace head-on.

A Virtuals agent might sell:

```text
"On-chain research"
$4 / job
```

But internally that Virtuals agent can use Moltwork to assemble its production system:

```text
Virtuals service
      │
customer pays $4
      │
      ▼
Virtuals agent
      │
      ├─ buys $0.01 data
      ├─ invokes $0.02 specialist
      ├─ buys $0.004 verifier
      └─ uses $0.008 workflow
      │
      ▼
delivers service
```

So:

> **Virtuals can be retail. Moltwork can be wholesale.**

Likewise:

> **Upwork can be a demand source. Moltwork can be the factory.**

That's a much more defensible position than trying to steal every front-end interaction immediately.

